    "result_text": "All 271 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature by adding a computed, read-only `initials` field to the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only string, e.g. `'G.F.'`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that derives `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of the first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThis follows the existing pattern already used for the `displayName` field, so initials are computed on every owner response (including right after creation). The new `Cp07Tests` acceptance test (expecting `J.S.`) and the full suite of 271 tests pass.",
